course: dictionary
lesson: 15482
title: Strictness: firm, fair and exact
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Strictness is a noun, a naming word for the quality of being strict. A strict person makes people follow the rules exactly and does not allow bad behaviour. «The strictness of the new head teacher surprised everyone, because she checked every uniform at the gate.» The clues are checked, every and uniform, so strictness means firm rule-keeping.
explain: Strictness is not always unkind. «Her strictness about homework meant that every child in her class finished their reading each night.» Here the strictness is firm but fair, because it helps the children learn. Ask yourself: is the person being firm, or unkind? The sentence will tell you.
explain: Strictness can also mean being exact and precise. «The strictness of the library rule meant it closed at exactly five o'clock, not one minute later.» The clue is exactly, so this strictness is about precision. To check any meaning, swap in firmness or exactness and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Strictness is a noun, and it is uncountable: you say «great strictness», not «a strictness».
fact: «Strictness» means being strict: making people follow rules exactly and not allowing bad behaviour.
fact: «Strictness» can also mean being exact and precise, like the strictness of a rule or a meaning.
fact: Strictness is often paired with kindness: «strictness and kindness» together can make a teacher fair and firm.
fact: «Strict» is the adjective, and «strictness» is the noun made from it, so look for the word strict when you need its root.
exercise: «The teacher's strictness meant nobody talked during the test.» What does strictness mean here? | Being very quiet | Forgetting about the test | *Making everyone follow the rules firmly | Playing games in class
exercise: «The strictness of the library rule meant it closed at exactly five o'clock, not one minute later.» What does strictness suggest here? | Being sad about closing time | *Being exact and precise | Being angry at the librarian
exercise: Which pair of words from the lessons shows strictness and kindness working together? | Homework and bedtime | Strictness and noise | *Strictness and kindness | Uniform and gate
test: «Her strictness made the whole class line up quietly before going out.» What does strictness mean? | Forgetting about lines | *Making people follow the rules firmly | Playing games | Being very quiet
test: Which word is the noun for being strict? | strict | stricter | strictly | *strictness
exam: Priya says strictness always means being unkind. What is the best answer? | Strictness is a type of food | Strictness means being sleepy | *No, strictness can be fair and firm, as in «strictness and kindness» | Yes, strictness is always unkind
